From fb794bb4ba50f7dc95d2afb5966e8b4d1a9be070 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:34:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the dictionary parse and add tap-to-lookup on the player
 subtitles

Two related fixes for the word-lookup feature:

The Youdao parser never produced dictionary senses: the sense text
sits at trs[i].tr[0].l.i (the tr element is an array), but the code
read it one level short, so every lookup only ever showed the web
translations. The structure was verified against the live API before
fixing (and the whole parse path re-validated against a captured
response: phonetics, exam labels, word forms and web translations
all resolve).

The player now also supports tapping a word directly on the bilingual
subtitles while watching - the actual tap-to-lookup feature. While
the controls are hidden the subtitle view is the topmost touchable
view, so it sees every touch first: a tap that hits a word of the
original layer takes the gesture and opens the dictionary popup;
every other touch returns false and flows on to the player gestures
untouched (tap-to-show-controls, double-tap seek, swipes). The gate
is re-evaluated on every touch-down, so nothing needs syncing when
the controls appear or the player locks. Hit-testing reuses the
StaticLayouts the draw already builds (getLineForVertical +
getOffsetForHorizontal plus word-boundary expansion), with a little
slack so thin lines stay tappable.

The dictionary popup itself moved into a shared WordDialogHelper, now
used by both the bilingual reader and the player.
